    "masterComponentSetNodeId": "519:3573",
    "masterComponentSetName": "Input-multiselect",
    "note": "This extraction targets the real master COMPONENT_SET (519:3573) supplied directly, resolved via figma_get_component_for_development_deep (Plugin API). All 5 declared variant children were found and traversed. FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN was expired for this session, so all REST-backed tools (figma_get_file_data, figma_get_component, figma_get_component_image, non-deep figma_get_component_for_development, figma_search_components) were not used; only Plugin-API-backed tools (figma_get_component_for_development_deep, figma_get_variables, figma_capture_screenshot) were used. mainComponent references for nested INSTANCEs were not exposed by the deep tool in this session (same limitation as the prior pass), so composition matches are based on Figma instance/layer names cross-referenced against klp-components.json, not resolved component keys."
  },
  "anatomy": [
    {
      "part": "root",
      "element": "div",
      "notes": "Outer wrapper stacking the trigger box above the (visually overflowing) open dropdown panel. Transparent - no fill of its own."
    },
    {
      "part": "trigger",
      "element": "div",
      "notes": "The label + input-box trigger region. Backed by an INSTANCE named 'Input' with componentProperties Size=Small; State varies per variant (Focused/Default/Filled - see each variant's layers.trigger.literals.state).",
      "klpComponent": "input",
      "klpComponentProps": {
        "size": "small"
      },
      "figmaInstance": {
        "name": "Input",
        "key": null
      }
    },
    {
      "part": "trigger-label",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "Label text above the input box, e.g. 'Label of the input'."
    },
    {
      "part": "trigger-info-icon",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "Optional info icon next to the trigger label. Hidden when the Info icon boolean prop is false (visible=true in all 5 captured variants)."
    },
    {
      "part": "input-box",
      "element": "div",
      "notes": "The bordered, rounded box (inside trigger's Content region) that holds the chips/placeholder and the chevron affordance. Border color follows the nested Input instance's State variant (bd/brand when Focused/Filled, bd/default when Default)."
    },
    {
      "part": "chip",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "One removable chip per selected value, repeated (2x in Filled, 4x in Full, 0x in Empty). Backed by an INSTANCE named 'badges' with variant Type=Tertiary/Size=Small/Style=Light.",
      "klpComponent": "badges",
      "klpComponentProps": {
        "badgeType": "tertiary",
        "size": "small",
        "badgeStyle": "light"
      },
      "figmaInstance": {
        "name": "badges",
        "key": null
      }
    },
    {
      "part": "chip-label",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "Chip text label, e.g. 'Label'. Not rendered in Content=Empty."
    },
    {
      "part": "chip-remove-icon",
      "element": "button",
      "notes": "X icon button inside each chip to deselect that value. Not rendered in Content=Empty."
    },
    {
      "part": "placeholder",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "Placeholder text shown in place of chips when Content=Empty (e.g. 'This is the placeholder or input content'). Hidden/not rendered in Filled and Full variants (a sibling '.typeofcontent' instance swaps between showing chips vs. this placeholder text)."
    },
    {
      "part": "chevron-icon",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "Chevron affordance at the right edge of the input-box. Points down (chevron-down) when State=Open, and right (chevron-right) when State=Close - captured literally from the Figma layer names 'Icon/Chevron-down' / 'Icon/Chevron-right' per variant; verify this is intentional design behavior (not simply an authoring inconsistency) with design before implementing a rotate-on-toggle affordance instead."
    },
    {
      "part": "dropdown",
      "element": "div",
      "notes": "The options panel. Backed by an INSTANCE named 'ActionSheet_Menu' with variant Type=Checkbox - each row wraps an 'Input Checkbox' instance (Checkbox + Label), grouped into sections with a title and a chevron-right disclosure affordance, separated by a divider line. Visible only when State=Open; hidden (visible=false, no boundVariables reported) when State=Close. The nested Checkbox reuse (klp 'checkbox' component) and the section/item/separator structure are internal to action-sheet-menu's own spec - not modeled as separate anatomy parts here since the whole subtree is delegated to the action-sheet-menu instance.",
      "klpComponent": "action-sheet-menu",
      "klpComponentProps": {
        "type": "checkbox"
      },
      "figmaInstance": {
